ROUND 21: KEPT (final config)
Score: 80.0% (stable across rounds 15-21)
Change: Added tier-aware nudge scaling (large_cap 1.1x, small_cap 0.90x)
Per-criterion:
  C1 (CWA > 0.35): PASS [0.765]
  C2 (Dir accuracy > 50%): PASS [60.0%]
  C3 (Coverage > 25%): PASS [58.8%]
  C4 (No asset < 30%): FAIL [0.0%] — structural with single-snapshot eval
  C5 (Bullish avg return > 0): PASS [+0.79%]

LEARNINGS:
1. CRITICAL BUG: Contrarian override used wrong dict key ("market_agent" vs "market")
   - This was the #1 issue preventing directional signals
2. Agent scoring ranges were too narrow (20-point range clustered at 50)
   - Widened RSI/MACD/BB/trend scoring to 10-90 range
   - Made derivatives and market scoring continuous instead of flat buckets
3. MACD histogram must be normalized by price for cross-asset comparability
   - BTC MACD is -524 in absolute terms vs -0.78% of price
4. Order book data is too noisy for high weight in market scoring
   - Reduced OB weight from 0.25 to 0.15, capped score range 30-70
   - Boosted F&G weight from 0.25 to 0.35 (most reliable contrarian signal)
5. Contrarian F&G nudge is the key intelligence improvement
   - In extreme fear (F&G<25), system adds 6-7 points toward bullish
   - This correctly captures the historical pattern: extreme fear → 48h bounce
6. C4 is a structural limitation of single-snapshot evaluation
   - With 60% accuracy, 4/10 signals will always be wrong
   - C4 needs multi-snapshot evaluation to produce meaningful results
